\newlabel{fig:motivation}{{1}{16}{Motivation: Decoder computation produces spatially localized prediction flips. While the full decoder corrects certain errors of the efficient baseline (positive flips), it also alters previously correct predictions (negative flips) near high-entropy organ boundaries, demonstrating non-uniform spatial contribution}{figure.1}{}}
